    -- verifier's EXECUTE fails closed — the desired outcome). The slot and claim guards are
    -- SECURITY DEFINER, P-owned, for the reason recorded at their definition site: ordinary
    -- DIRECT client inserts must pass, cannot hold the A verifier's counterpart-only EXECUTE,
    -- and must not be granted it — so the guard itself carries the exact product-owner identity
    -- its one P→A call executes under. The secdef column pins that split so neither shape can
